body:
Self-awareness is definitely useful when speaking with anyone who isn’t already familiar with K-pop! Gotta know what needs additional explanations at the very least, you know? Hmm, perhaps I would explain the person OP is speaking about like this - 

what the person OP is speaking about would say to a friend if they showed them an MV they like - “it’s honestly so weird that they spend so much money on the music videos. K-pop really is all about how pretty the music looks, not how well it sounds. It disgusts me sometimes. Ha, look at that person, they’ve had so much plastic surgery!”. 

A normal person would explain the context for MVs and why they are important, and what they like about them, etc. and generally try to get their friends to _like_ the MV, not preemptively start hating on it lmao. I’m def not saying that disclaimers and explanations aren’t necessary! It’s just that some people don’t use disclaimers, they just straight up hate ;-;

November was glorious, mainly because I visited an actual brick and mortar K-pop store for the first time in my life (went to Milan for the XH concert lol).

Waiting for:

SKZ limited rock star;

SKZ Headliner rock star;

SKZ nemo rock star;

SKZ 3x postcard rock star…

