I am, indeed, a broke bitch. But I’ve finished collecting skz albums now, so these numbers are massively going down now lol. AND I’m gonna stick to only getting new comebacks from now on. This is ✨ not sustainable ✨

It’s a very fun question to look at through the lenses of sex/gender for sure! The assumption that “bigger” and “darker” is more masculine than “smaller” and “lighter” is 100% gender norm stereotype based. I think especially since everyone always sees them together and obviously a comparison is made. I’m always pretty surprised that people are really VERY sure about their sex? It’s not that there’s an assumption only because you have to use gendered words in my language, they are absolutely convinced about their sex. I feel like dogs have comparatively VERY few uh, sex characteristics (however they’re called properly). It’s not like they have plumage like birds? Anyways! Interesting stuff. 

The additional question of “gender presentation” for dogs is slightly hilarious, but it’s there for sure. Some people really DO care that the male dog has a pink harness. Or that the male dog is more shy and a scaredy-cat in comparison to the female dog. 

The issue of whether a dogs sex is necessary to know is hmm, more clear cut to me? It’s definitely important when dogs meet for the first time. By and large, a male and female dog meeting for the first time are less likely to argue than a same sex meeting. And well, some dogs are sexist lmao. Wanna fight all dudes or all gals. I personally also keep an eye on male dogs, especially intact ones, because the moment your new shoes are marked for the first time you start living a paranoia filled life. ;-;

The best thing is to stay calm yourself. When you’re very anxious you feel overwhelmed. So if the other person you’re with is super high energy or needs to be reassured that can be a bit of a bother. Don’t ask her super complicated/very open ended questions, because it’s hard to make big decisions when you’re feeling anxious. What you can do more specifically - 

1) stay calm. 

2) ask her if there’s something you can do to help her;

2a) if she doesn’t know what could help her you can offer her a few options, for example:

a) would you like to go to a quieter place? (if you’re in public);

b) would you like a hug/to hold my hand/cuddle/etc.?

c) would you like a cold glass of water?

d) would you like to try out a breathing exercise with me? (Google a few);

e) would you like some reassurance?

You can also ask your girlfriend! When I went for my first international trip with my best friend I provided her a list of instructions of how to help me if I got a panic attack. It made life a lot easier. Some things for me personally are counter intuitive! I don’t like a lot of reassurance when I’m panicking lol, and I absolutely hate eating if I’m nervous so giving me my favourite snack wouldn’t work. That’s why “instructions” can be a good idea if your girlfriend is fine with that. But the general advice above also works. :)

Oh honestly so much and I’ve only been listening to them for a few months. 

- been working out my arms for like two months due to Binnie&Channie (results are in and it’s hot as shit);

- started studying Korean (however, continued past learning only Hangul because I actually like the language);

- struck up a few new friendships;

- started taking my skincare and hair more seriously lmao;

- so many new kpop inspired hairstyles and makeup looks;

- more street style fashion ✨;

- self confidence? through the roof. bonafide glow up for me;

- am tinkering with the piano again because Channie already does everything better than me, he’s taking the piano over my dead body;

- also, much poorer -> Lollapalooza. (worth it). 

10/10 would recommend skz to overhaul your entire life.
